    "result_text": "Tests remain green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI agreed with all three findings \u2014 they were doc-vs-code incoherences my change introduced (the `@Column`/`@Transient` Javadoc in this codebase is treated as first-class, and I'd updated the parallel OpenAPI/normalizer docs but missed these internal ones). Fixes applied:\n\n1. **`Owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`** \u2014 rewrote the Javadoc to describe the new soft-match rule (earlier non-deleted owner with matching `soundex(lastName)` + postcode but differing `identityKey`; exact-match is a 409 that never reaches the flag), dropping the stale `householdId`/`sharesHousehold` wording.\n\n2. **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 removed `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` from the household-consumer list (householdId now feeds only size and membership-cap) and deleted the `sharesHousehold` suppression claim, pointing duplicate detection at the `identityKey` via `DetectOwnerDuplicate`/`DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate`.\n\n3. **`HouseholdMembers`** \u2014 removed `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` from the list of steps sharing the member definition, since it now inlines its own soundex+postcode scan rather than calling `HouseholdMembers.of(...)`.\n\nAll are Javadoc-only; executable behavior is unchanged and acceptance tests still pass.",
