    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe executable structure is clean and idiomatic: `DetectOwnerDuplicate` follows the `Detect<E>Duplicate` naming with one public `service` method, a checked exception plus escalation-YAML/handler triple, and correct pipeline placement; the inlined `findAll()` scans in both detect classes match the codebase's established convention (`CountOwnerNamesakes` inlines the same skip-self/skip-deleted loop rather than using `HouseholdMembers`, which is reserved for householdId-keyed consumers); the hand-rolled `sha256Hex` mirrors the existing per-function hashing in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`/`AssignOwnerHousehold`; and reusing `Owner.soundex` from both the entity key and the soft-match keeps the phonetic definition in one place. No complaint there.\n\nThe problem is coherence: this change treats the (very heavy) javadoc as part of the unit of work \u2014 it carefully updated `openapi.yml` (three blocks), `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` and `Owner.getIdentityKey()` \u2014 but left three internal docs describing the *removed* household-based behavior, so they now actively misdescribe the rewired control flow. A maintainer reading them would be misled.\n\nConcrete, actionable findings:\n\n1. `Owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` javadoc (model/Owner.java:256\u2013262) still says the flag is \"keyed off the shared householdId (same lastName and postcode). A declared household member (created with `sharesHousehold` true) is never flagged; any other owner joining an existing household is allowed but flagged.\" This is the old semantics \u2014 the new `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` keys off soundex(lastName)+postcode with a differing identityKey and no longer reads `sharesHousehold`. Notably the parallel `possibleDuplicate` block in openapi.yml *was* updated; this getter was missed. Update it to match.\n\n2. `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` class javadoc (lines ~18\u201323) lists `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` among the \"household consumers [that] key off\" the computed householdId, and states `sharesHousehold` \"only suppresses the possible-duplicate flag for a declared member (see `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate`).\" Both are now false: the rewritten step no longer keys off householdId and no longer consults `sharesHousehold` at all (suppression is gone). Drop `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` from the consumer list and remove the suppression claim.\n\n3. `HouseholdMembers.java` class javadoc names `DetectOwnerPossibleDuplicate` as one of \"the steps that reason over a household\" sharing its member definition, but that step no longer calls `HouseholdMembers.of(...)` (it inlines its own soundex+postcode scan). Remove it from that list so the helper's stated consumers stay accurate.\n\nThese are doc-vs-code incoherences the change itself introduced; fixing them keeps the documentation (which this codebase treats as first-class and the change otherwise diligently maintained) consistent with the new logic.",
